{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_hpx63osbficsa5ybtnkpjbfm6qeyegy76t7cpq4qtroj3mt7yoda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The translation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C coroutine library (which uses `ucontext` for stackful coroutine context switching with a shared stack/copy-on-yield design) into Rust without using FFI/`libc`.\n\n### Approach\n\nSince Rust doesn't have stable `ucontext` access in the standard library and the rules forbid FFI to libc, I simulated the cooperative coroutine semantics using:\n\n- **One OS thread per coroutine** spawned on the first `coroutine_resume`.\n- **Rendezvous via two `sync_channel(0)` pairs** — one for scheduler→coroutine (\"here is the schedule pointer, run\") and one for coroutine→scheduler (\"I yielded\" / \"I am done\"). Because the bound is 0, `send` and `recv` synchronize like a context switch — exactly one side runs at a time, matching the cooperative semantics of the C version.\n- **A global `OnceLock<Mutex<HashMap<usize, ChannelPair>>>` registry** keyed by the heap address of each `Coroutine`, so a suspended coroutine's channel/thread pair can be found again across resume calls (the `Schedule`/`Coroutine` definitions are fixed and have no place for the channel state).\n- **A `thread_local!` slot** lets `coroutine_yield` send back to the scheduler and wait to be resumed without needing extra fields on `Schedule`.\n\n### Behavior preserved\n\n- READY → RUNNING on first resume; RUNNING → SUSPEND on yield; resume of suspended → RUNNING again; on coroutine return: slot cleared, `nco--`, `running = -1` (matches C).\n- `coroutine_new` doubles the table when `nco >= cap`; otherwise scans `(i + nco) % cap` to find a free slot.\n- `coroutine_status` returns `COROUTINE_DEAD` for empty slots; `coroutine_resume` is a no-op (silent return) for empty slots.\n- `coroutine_close` reaps any still-running coroutine threads and frees all coroutines.\n\n### Verification\n\nI added integration tests in `tests/integration.rs`:\n1. `matches_c_test_output` — replays the original `c_src/tests/test.c` scenario and verifies the exact interleaved output sequence.\n2. `growth_when_capacity_exceeded` — creates 20 coroutines (> `DEFAULT_COROUTINE` = 16) to exercise the resize path.\n\nBoth tests pass; `cargo build` is clean."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":300,"cache_read_input_tokens":31431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":300,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b66984a8-1870-4094-9854-bdbcbdaad47b","uuid":"359a6cae-aedb-4f33-aaad-3bc1442852fd"}
